-- A BOOLEAN rule written as DECIDE clauses over a MAYBE input. The ladder
-- breaks a column down into questions only when it matches an enum value or a
-- literal; this one matches JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING, so the whole
-- rule is one box. `l4 verify` says it did not analyse it, rather than that it
-- found nothing.
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `flag is set` (JUST TRUE)  IS TRUE
DECIDE `flag is set` (JUST FALSE) IS FALSE
DECIDE `flag is set` NOTHING      IS FALSE
